	(hierarchical_label "DBG_TX"
		(shape input)
		(at 177.8 74.93 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "ce81a090-bbaa-5c9a-b81c-ac5e57b5916c")
	)
	(text "PINOUT - standard ARM Cortex Debug 10-pin order on 2.54 mm pitch, so a\n2x5 SWD probe cable plugs straight on:\n  1 VTref (+3V3)   2 SWDIO      3 GND     4 SWCLK    5 GND\n  6 SWO            7 DBG_RX     8 DBG_TX  9 GND     10 nRESET\n\nPins 7 and 8 are KEY / NC on the ARM pinout and are reused here for the\nUSART3 console (REQ-AR-15 and the block diagram both put SWD and UART on\nONE header). They are SWD-safe: an SWD probe drives only 2, 4 and 10 and\nreads 6. This part is SWD-only anyway - the .ioc sets Trace_Asynchronous_SW,\nso PB4/PB3 are not JTAG. The 100R series resistors make a mis-plugged JTAG\nprobe or a shorted console pin a nuisance rather than damage.\n\nDBG_TX / DBG_RX keep the .ioc net names: DBG_TX is the STM32 OUTPUT\n(USART3_TX, PD8), DBG_RX the STM32 INPUT (USART3_RX, PD9).\nnRESET is MCU_nRESET, generated in the mcu block (which owns its 100 nF,\nits push button and its test point - producer-owns-the-break, DEC-0007)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 24.13 84.46 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "a6619c14-faa8-53a5-8b98-35b97dff613e")
	)
	(rectangle (start 210.82 30.48) (end 320.04 133.35)
		(stroke (width 0.2) (type solid))
		(fill (type none))
		(uuid "3e215d29-fa63-5490-a563-9501a4c1cb07")
	)
