	(text "Six through-hole GND loops, spread across the board so an oscilloscope\nground clip is never far from the signal hook being probed. The house\nstandard asks for these wherever TestPointHook is used, and the block\nsheets use hooks on I2C1, SPI2, SPI3 and the fault lines."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 326.39 114.3 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "8b9d8b0c-6ac7-54dd-a1dc-024cc568781d")
	)
	(rectangle (start 22.86 139.7) (end 407.67 190.5)
		(stroke (width 0.2) (type solid))
		(fill (type none))
		(uuid "ae9cb216-7801-5514-80c9-9a304cee2094")
	)
	(text "SHEET NOTES"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 24.13 140.97 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.6 1.6) (bold yes)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "1004476f-416c-5d14-a987-069ed3a84dbc")
	)
	(text "BLOCK: test_debug - system-level bring-up hardware that no functional block owns (DEC-0007).\nEverything here observes; nothing here generates a rail or a signal, so this sheet owns no isolation link\nor current break. Per-block test points, links and breaks stay in the sheet that produces the net.\n\nROOT SHEET NEEDS - hierarchical labels this sheet exposes, all of them shared with the mcu block:\n  SWDIO, SWCLK, SWO, MCU_nRESET, DBG_TX, DBG_RX.\nThe rails (+5V, +3V3, +3V3A, GND) are global power nets and need no sheet pins.\nAll six are sheet pins on the test_debug block of the root sheet now, wired straight across to the mcu\nblock: the integration pass that closed DEC-0009 drew them, and project ERC is clean at severity-all.\nSee docs/decisions/actuator-sch-mcu.md for the full list and directions."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 145.42 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "0c65ad11-422b-584a-bd59-af0771417da2")
	)
